// Visual Studio's way to the semantic tokens (docs/editors.md, "Colors"), for tests\lsp.ps1 on a
// copy of tests\lsp\program: with initializationOptions' semanticColors the client is offered no
// semanticTokensProvider (its extension draws the tokens), and kpp/semanticTokensChanged follows
// each check. shapes.kpp's tokens: the global units::scale has the modifier globalScope (8).
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"rootUri":"$ROOT","capabilities":{},"initializationOptions":{"semanticColors":true}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"initialized","params":{}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"textDocument/semanticTokens/full","params":{"textDocument":{"uri":"$ROOT/shapes.kpp"}}}
// words.kpp's tokens: kpp's own words are kppKeyword (12) where the parser takes them: `when`,
// `implicit`, `This`, `fallthrough;`, `assert(`, `suite`, `depends`, `test`, and in the test (skipped
// without --tests) the statements `check(`, `require(`, `fail(` and `requireThrows<`. The method
// check stays a method (11) where it is called, `g.check(3)` and `g.check(kind)`.
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":5,"method":"textDocument/semanticTokens/full","params":{"textDocument":{"uri":"$ROOT/words.kpp"}}}
// The legend the extension maps the tokens by (kpp/semanticTokensLegend): the capability's.
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"method":"kpp/semanticTokensLegend","params":{}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"shutdown"}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"exit"}
